implementation_plan.detail:
Chair ownership already persists through Inventory (the setup tab). Seated state is not saved: loading and map entry always start standing. Add a playtest scenario (game/tools/playtest/scenarios/test_h_chair.gd) that runs the whole loop with no console:
- accept 1012, break Wooden Boxes for 3 Screws and 3 Boards, turn in, receive 522;
- open the Set-up tab, sit, take damage first, watch HP rise by 40 per 10 s;
- press a move key to stand;
- save, reload, sit again.

summary:
AP is canonical and verified. Everything else in this domain is still placeholder or missing.

Natural HP recovery exists, but it implements the Iteration Two adaptation (game/data/misostory/combat.json:60-67, NaturalRecoveryRule.step at game/scripts/core/character/natural_recovery_rule.gd:58-67), not the owner's rule. The adaptation restores 10 HP after 10 s of uninterrupted rest, and only after 5 s out of combat (delay_s). Any ineligible tick (moving, airborne, climbing, hitstun, warping), full HP, or any combat event (an attack started, a monster hit, a miss or a guard) resets the timer to 0 instead of pausing it. The owner's rule is: 10 HP per 10 s of accumulated eligible time; eligible means standing completely still or sitting; walking, jumping and attacking pause the timer without resetting it; no combat delay; never above Max HP. The unit tests (test_natural_recovery.gd:43-50) and the regen playtest still assert the old reset/delay behaviour, so they must be rewritten.

MeowDB documents no natural MP recovery anywhere in the 1050-file cache. MP comes only from consumables (Orange 239 +50, sold by Lucy; Lemon 240; Blue Potion 273) and the full level-up heal (an adaptation). The current "no MP regen" matches MeowDB's silence and must stay an explicit source gap, not be inferred from the HP rule.

Sitting and chairs are missing.
- The X binding ("sit") exists, but nothing reads it, and the controls panel hides it (controls_panel.gd:16).
- PlayerController has only GROUND/AIR/CLIMB states (player_controller.gd:47); there is no sit state or pose.
- The Green Relaxer (item 522, Setup, setup.hp_recovery_bonus 30 / interval 10) is reward data only:
  - quest 1012 gives it;
  - ItemDef parses the setup data and the tooltip prints "While sitting: +30 HP every 10 s";
  - the inventory window refuses to use Setup items (inventory_window.gd:178 NOT_USABLE);
  - quickslots accept consumables only (quickslots.gd:45).

Beginner skills are missing as a feature, although the canonical data is complete:
- beginner.json skills[] holds ids, max level 3, per-level MP and shell costs, damage, HP-over-time, speed and cooldowns;
- attack_speed.json three_snails holds the 800 ms base, 810 ms at Normal 6;
- attack_styles.json three_snails_targeting holds the stepped 50-300 px band, 28 px aim height, 1:4 widening, 100 px up / 44 px down;
- movement.json holds the Nimble Feet +10.

Only fragments exist: CombatFormula.resolve_fixed_damage for Three Snails with combat.json fixed_damage_skills flags plus one unit test, the CharacterState.skills/effects fields (persisted, never written), and the K binding (reserved, hidden). There is no skill window, no SP spending, no casting, no timed-effect/buff system and no cooldowns. SP is granted correctly (1 per level-up at levels 2-10, 0 after 10 by adaptation; verified in unit tests and the real-game test_c), but it piles up unspendable (the baseline test_c ends at level 8 with 7 SP).

Smaller problems: docs/canonical/README.md:74 points to a non-existent game/data/misostory/recovery.json, and test_c_progression.gd still says "no natural HP regeneration exists" (lines 20 and 1100).

implementation_plan.detail:
Create a PlayerSkills node next to PlayerCombat, sharing its lockout and AttackLockInput.
- Three Snails:
  - target search: the stepped band (start 50 px, 20 px steps, 28 px aim height, widening 1 px per 4 px, up to 300 px forward, 100 px up / 44 px down) in a new CombatReach helper, given depth across the facing by isometric_reach.attack_box_depth_px;
  - target choice: nearest first, 1 target (MeleeQuery-style pick);
  - damage: CombatFormula.resolve_fixed_damage(..., "0001000") applied through MonsterSystem.apply_player_hit;
  - lockout: CombatFormula timing on the 800 ms base at the weapon tier (810 ms at Normal 6);
  - projectile flight is presentation only (flight time is a gap).
- Recovery: adds a heal-over-time effect and starts the 120 s cooldown.
- Nimble Feet: adds speed +10 for 10/20/30 s and starts the 180 s cooldown.
- A cast counts as 'attacking' for regen (step 3).

New game/scripts/ui/minimap/minimap_view.gd (MisoMinimapView, a Control). The static layer is drawn once per map as an ArrayMesh of the projected ground triangles with tier colours from MisoTheme (draw_mesh), plus outline, routes and climbables. The dynamic layer, redrawn at 10-15 Hz, holds:
- portal glyphs (swirl ring for edge, door rectangle for door) with an outward chevron and a small destination label, or a hover tooltip on dense maps like 000001000 (8 exits);
- shop coin badges, using MisoCoinIcon styling;
- NPC dots carrying the QuestMarker STYLES glyph from NpcInteraction.marker(npc_id) via WorldUiServices.npc_talk(ctx), and a coin or anchor icon for Shopkeeper or Transport;
- the player arrow at ctx.player.global_position with the player's facing; clamped to the frame edge with a '-> <dest>' tag while MapSession.trail_destination is not empty.
New game/scripts/ui/minimap/minimap.gd (MisoMinimap, PanelContainer). It has a MisoTheme title strip ('<street> · <name>', plus ' [<map_id>]' while Debug.overlay_enabled) and setup(ctx) via MisoUiEnv.from_ctx. It handles toggle_minimap (M) in _unhandled_input and stays quiet under env.is_modal_active(), the same rule as windows_root.gd. M cycles expanded / title-only, or toggles, per the open question.
Subscriptions: Events.map_entered (rebuild), quest_started / quest_progressed / quest_completed / quest_forfeited, item_gained / item_lost, leveled_up (markers), MapSession.trail_changed, Debug.overlay_toggled, Game.character_replaced, game_loaded.
Place it top-left (16, 16; about 300x200 px, scaled from the map's iso aspect), below the debug overlay's layer; the overlay is top-right anyway. Presentation constants stay in code, per the UI.md convention. New game/scenes/ui/minimap.tscn; add {'name': 'Minimap', 'scene': 'res://scenes/ui/minimap.tscn', 'parent': 'ui_root'} to SubsystemInstaller.DEFAULT_SUBSYSTEMS after the HUD.

